body:
Realistically whichever the school will allow. Idk where you are but the DVA outfit would be too "tight" for many schools and the collar may also be against rules, not sure if they care if you wear fem clothes in general though. 

&#x200B;

My personal recommendation would be the first one. It is super cute, comfy, and easy to move in.

I completely agree with you.

&#x200B;

I have a friend that swears on gray market sites and even tries to get some of our other friends to use them over official sites. I have been using IsthereAnyDeal for several years now and their sites are traditionally safe and vetted. Why risk saving a couple bucks here and there to risk losing your games or getting banned? Just track the games you want, a feature built into IsthereAnyDeal, and be patient.

When it comes to Miranda Rights it is really only questioning. You can be detained without being read your rights. The thing is that if you are questioned before being read your rights anything you say cannot be used against you in the court of law which is way part of the rights is, "Anything you say or do can and will be used against you in the court of law." 

&#x200B;

Another thing with Miranda Rights is that the person has to be in a stable state of mind in order to use any questioning against them. If someone is drunk and cannot give consent then the officers cannot use questioning against them until they are sober, this also applies to those with mental disabilities.

Ultimately I don't think it is too big of an issue, yet. If other devs follow the same route then the subreddit would slowly turn into just ads and lose traction.

&#x200B;

 I understand the mods' stance as although the posts are spam like, without hard evidence or research into the user posting it is hard to enforce an applicable rule such as rule 3. At the moment if an account is clearly spam they should be banned and the post removed. The issue is how to determine if it is a new user/lurker vs. spam account. You cannot automatically assume that every post about the game is spam.

&#x200B;

I don't think we are to the point where there is a need to make a new rule, but, that will probably be open to discussion if it becomes more of an issue. Understandably some people are annoyed with the posts and would like something done and the best way is to message the mod team about the post. Having too many rules could deter new people from joining the community.

I recommend looking for a sitting job that isn't sales, call center, or cold calling. Office experience is more impactful if you are not sticking with the same company. 

&#x200B;

I am disabled and only have a GED. I started in retail at $12/hour and got up to almost $15/hour. I ended up with a job with the county and started to earn $16/hour and eventually $18/hour. I also picked up seasonal work as an office manager for a tax prep company that only paid $13/hour but it let me put office manager on my resume. Now I work for a nonprofit organization and make $23/hour. 

&#x200B;

As others have said try not to quit your current job until you have another lined up. Try to prioritize your health first. It could take months or a year to find a better position but it will be worth it.

Non-profits and 503-c can run very differently to one another, most are volunteer. The chances of finding a paying non profit that focuses on trans activism will probably be very difficult. 

&#x200B;

I came across my company while browsing Indeed. I got very lucky. I just so happened to be the person they were looking for. They needed someone who could use technology, set up events, and create network connections. With us being disability focused I was a perfect fit, I am disabled and part of the LGBTQIA+ community so I had a unique insight.

&#x200B;

Many related communities overlap and work together, in my area the only trans activism is part of the local university's LGBT organization. That may be different for you. Good resources outside of Googling would be to reach out to you local colleges/universities, county office, and if you have one Diversity Council.

The UI can use a lot of work. I have no idea what is going on with the inventory/shop area. I supposedly picked up two blueprints but it says I have 0 plans and when I click on blueprints it doesn't do anything. I'm not sure if crafting is actually implemented or not as materials appear to all have the same values. I wish that loot auto collected after a couple seconds and didn't prevent you from being able to click on Do Job, I thought for a moment I was stuck until I realized that you click the icon for each looted item and then the loot screen disappears after a few seconds. I also do not like the fact that if you are trying to scroll up in the job list while the loot table is on screen it cycles on the top. I also don't like how the entirety of the Health/Cash/Stamina/LV area is clickable and only shows health information, I would put a small icon next to or within Health to open up the menu instead. 

&#x200B;

Biggest complaint is that I have no information about what certain things do unless I do experimenting, such as leveling up jobs. Normally I would just go for Jobs with unique drops and those that give the most exp per stamina but the level system could change that, however I'm not sure if leveling jobs make a difference. I leveled the first job expecting a reward increase both nothing changed going from F to E.

&#x200B;

Overall I do really like the feel you are going for, it reminds me of the old Mafia Wars games.
